      "slug": "fn-declare-environments",
      "capability": "cap-environment-setup",
      "intents": [
        "bi-2"
      ],
      "one_line": "Declares which environments the project has, at least dev, testing and pre-production and never production, and for each one its data, its size, its network, who can reach it and its own settings, so every deployment and every test runs in a place that was set up on purpose.",
      "doc": "software-delivery-planning/environment-setup/fn-declare-environments/feature.md",
      "identified_by": ""
    },
    {
      "id": "fn-build-environment",
      "kind": "feature",
      "mode": "new",
      "slug": "fn-build-environment",
      "capability": "cap-environment-setup",
      "intents": [
        "bi-2"
      ],
      "one_line": "When a deployment needs an environment that is not built yet, builds it on its own from the one design of the underlying technology and its declaration, after a person's yes, checks that it answers, and from then on keeps it apart from the others until a person asks to take it down.",
      "doc": "software-delivery-planning/environment-setup/fn-build-environment/feature.md",
      "identified_by": ""
    },
    {
      "id": "fn-update-environments",
      "kind": "feature",
      "mode": "new",
      "slug": "fn-update-environments",
      "capability": "cap-environment-setup",
      "intents": [
        "bi-2"
      ],
      "one_line": "When the project needs another environment, or an environment's data, size, network, access or settings must change, a person confirms an update, and what held before stays readable with why it changed.",
      "doc": "software-delivery-planning/environment-setup/fn-update-environments/feature.md",
      "identified_by": ""
    },
    {
      "id": "fn-dev-sandbox",
      "kind": "feature",
      "mode": "new",
      "slug": "fn-dev-sandbox",
      "capability": "cap-environment-setup",
      "intents": [
        "bi-2"
      ],
      "one_line": "Sets up a place on a builder's own machine where the builder runs the project's code while building it, with each part running on the machine itself and no container platform or cloud service needed, so a builder can try a change before it goes to dev.",
